;; Reviewed 2026-10-11 by the user (written by Claude, from the design,
;; the MACRO manual and the guest runs). Why this is right:
;; - Phase 16 step 5 (section 16, proposal 7): SYSTEM.LSH, ROT and BIT.
;;   The value is widened to a longword (a CHAR by MOVZBL, a word by
;;   MOVZWL, since a logical shift must not see a sign) or is a quadword
;;   in R0/R1 (HUGEINT); the result is narrowed back (MOVZBL, CVTWL).
;; - The count of LSH (ShiftCount, shared with ASH) is clamped to
;;   -64..64 unless its type cannot exceed that (a SHORTINT), since ASHL's
;;   and ASHQ's count is a signed byte; a HUGEINT count is clamped by its
;;   high longword first (0: unsigned compare of the low with 64; -1:
;;   unsigned compare with -64; otherwise the sign decides).
;; - LSH left is ASHL/ASHQ by the count. LSH right is logical, which the
;;   VAX has no instruction for: shift right by 1 (ASHL/ASHQ #-1), clear
;;   the sign bit of the (high) longword (BICL2 #^X80000000), then shift
;;   arithmetically by the count plus 1 (INCL). A constant count is folded
;;   into the second shift, LSH(l, -4) as #-1 and #-3, LSH(h, -40) as #-1
;;   and #-39.
;; - ROT of a longword is ROTL, its count n AND 31 (BICL3 #-32), which
;;   is n's floored modulo, so a negative n rotates right. A byte or word
;;   x has no rotate: x zero-extended times 2^w+1 (257, 65537) holds two
;;   copies of x; shifted left by n AND (w-1) and arithmetically right by w,
;;   its low w bits are x rotated (the MULL2 may set V, which traps only
;;   with IV in the entry mask, never set). ROT(i, -3) of a word is 13,
;;   ROT(l, 33) is 1.
;; - ROT of a HUGEINT calls POC_ROTQ (PocRtl.mar) with the addresses of
;;   x and of the count sign-extended to a quadword (ASHL #-31) through
;;   CALLG, as the other quadword routines; it returns R0/R1.
;; - BIT(a, n) is bit n of the memory at a, as voc reads it on a
;;   little-endian machine: BBC n, (Ra) is the VAX's variable bit field,
;;   any longword position from the byte at a. The BOOLEAN is CLRB, and
;;   INCB when the bit is set. A HUGEINT n is split: its byte offset
;;   (ASHQ #-3, low longword) added to a, its low three bits (BICL3 #-8)
;;   the position.
;; - ShiftsOut, run on the guest, prints what the LLVM build prints
;;   (output.expected), each case at each width.
; VaxShifts, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
	.TITLE	VAXSHIFTS
	.IDENT	/a06250420628208f/
	.PSECT	POC_CODE,  PIC,SHR,NOWRT,EXE,LONG
	.PSECT	POC_CONST, PIC,SHR,NOWRT,NOEXE,QUAD
	.PSECT	POC_DATA,  NOPIC,NOSHR,WRT,NOEXE,QUAD

; set once the module has been initialised
	.PSECT	POC_DATA
L_INITIALISED:
